From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:42:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/79] core lanes: opt-in head stops and joiners' first drafts
 in one batch

Two round-loop mechanisms MiaAI-Lab's Flash Next engine was tuned with, both off unless a family's
Model asks for them, so every other family runs as before:

- draft_stops / draft_stops_most: the head stops each chain by its own rule, so while at most that
  many streams are live every depth ask is the room's most drafts (Rule.stopsNow).
- join_batch: a joining stream's first token goes out at once and its first drafts wait for the next
  step, where every joiner drafts in one head batch (lanes/join_batch.zig).

Engine.activeCount moves to handover.zig and one depth test to head_stops_test.zig so engine.zig and
depth.zig stay within 600 lines.
